  "interpretation": [
    "The frozen E3G gate incorrectly made successful construction of a full dry-flux soil trial a prerequisite for discovering that the dry boundary mode is physically inadmissible.",
    "For B01, O13 and O14 the dry predictor is driven to the frozen top-head upper bound near -1e-8 cm and cannot satisfy the frozen mass residual tolerance; both candidate and reference show the same mechanism.",
    "B12 is a useful negative control: it can construct a numerically valid dry full-step trial, but the resulting trial is still complementarity-inadmissible and is therefore rejected before the ponded solve.",
    "The physical boundary admission question must be separated from whether a numerically valid state can be forced inside an already-inadmissible dry mode.",
    "Do not weaken the original E3G gate. Preserve it as negative evidence and test the corrected admission ordering in a separate E3G-R1 gate."
  ],
